;; A `(query …)` keyword the engine does not read is a load error and not a
;; silent no-op — M1c S1c.1.2. The keyword this file mistypes carries a *test*,
;; so a form that swallowed the typo would report success on a check nobody
;; ran, which is the one outcome the form exists to prevent.

(relation p Thing Place)
(p A H1)
(query :goal (p A ?h) :expct (model (p A H1)))
